:: Hopeless Cycle Cell Bandages Intro Talk
<<set _thermoDisable to true>><<effects>>
<<hopelessCycleEffects>>
<<if $hc.handLocation is "guardhouse">><<hcSuspicion 5>><</if>>
<span class="narration">The gaoler wanted to minimise contact, and getting the witch to keep still would be the best way. How did <<worldMale 'he' 'she'>> do it? Well...</span>
<br><br>

You take a deep breath. Speaking with prisoners is usually forbidden. What's more, <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>>'s a witch, <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> could snatch your voice right from your throat!
<br><br>

You decide that it's still your best chance to get <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> to cooperate. You tell <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> that you're trying to help <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>>, and that you need to remove <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> bandages to do so.
<br><br>

<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> stops squirming, <<worldFemale 'her' 'his'>> head moving to look at you again. "Hhh...hh..." <<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> seems to try and say something, but <<worldFemale 'she' 'he'>> only lets out a whimper.
<<worldFemale 'She' 'He'>> doesn't seem to understand you, merely reacting to the tone of your voice. Like a hound.
<br><br>

Tricks to make <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> seem more vulnerable, no doubt. Still, it did get <<worldFemale 'her' 'him'>> to stop cowering so much.
<br><br>

<<link [[붕대를 빨리 제거한다 (0:03)|Hopeless Cycle Cell Bandages Intro 2]]>><<pass 3>><<set $phase to 1>><<set $prisoner.love -= 1>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[붕대를 부드럽게 제거한다 (0:10)|Hopeless Cycle Cell Bandages Intro 2]]>><<pass 10>><<set $phase to 2>><<trauma 6>><</link>><<gtrauma>>
